  "description": "Given an array `nums` of `n` integers, return an array of all unique quadruplets `[nums[a], nums[b], nums[c], nums[d]]` such that `a`, `b`, `c`, and `d` are distinct indices and `nums[a] + nums[b] + nums[c] + nums[d] == target`. The order of the quadruplets does not matter.",
  "target": 0,
  "pseudocode": "function fourSum(nums, target):\n    sort(nums)\n    n = nums.length\n    results = []\n\n    for i from 0 to n - 4:\n        // Skip duplicate for i\n        if i > 0 and nums[i] == nums[i-1]:\n            continue\n\n        for j from i + 1 to n - 3:\n            // Skip duplicate for j\n            if j > i + 1 and nums[j] == nums[j-1]:\n                continue\n\n            left = j + 1\n            right = n - 1\n            target_two_sum = target - nums[i] - nums[j]\n\n            while left < right:\n                current_sum = nums[left] + nums[right]\n\n                if current_sum == target_two_sum:\n                    results.push([nums[i], nums[j], nums[left], nums[right]])\n                    // Skip duplicates for left\n                    while left < right and nums[left] == nums[left + 1]:\n                        left++\n                    // Skip duplicates for right\n                    while left < right and nums[right] == nums[right - 1]:\n                        right--\n                    left++\n                    right--\n                else if current_sum < target_two_sum:\n                    left++\n                else: // current_sum > target_two_sum\n                    right--\n    return results",
